# Registration for the two startup hooks in com.autox.config.env.
#
# spring.factories, not a META-INF/spring/*.imports file: the .imports mechanism is
# ImportCandidates, which Spring Boot uses for @AutoConfiguration only. EnvironmentPostProcessor
# and FailureAnalyzer are both loaded through SpringFactoriesLoader, which reads this file and
# nothing else. Registering them in an .imports file is silently ignored — no warning, no error,
# the hooks simply never run, which cost a debugging round here.
#
# Each post-processor declares its own getOrder(): the dotenv loader runs just before
# application.yml is read, the configuration check runs after everything.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.autox.config.env.DotenvEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.autox.config.env.RequiredConfigurationEnvironmentPostProcessor

org.springframework.boot.diagnostics.FailureAnalyzer=\
com.autox.config.env.MissingConfigurationFailureAnalyzer
